{title: Standing on the Promises}
{artist: R. Kelso Carter}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Traditional}
{key: C}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Standing on the promises of [F]Christ my [C]King
Through e[C]ternal ages let His [G7]praises [C]ring
[C]Glory in the highest, [F]I will shout and [C]sing
Standing on the [G7]promises of [C]God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Standing, standing
Standing on the [F]promises of God my [C]Saviour
[C]Standing, standing
I'm standing on the [G7]promises of [C]God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Standing on the promises that [F]cannot [C]fail
When the [C]howling storms of doubt and [G7]fear as[C]sail
By the [C]living Word of God I [F]shall pre[C]vail
Standing on the [G7]promises of [C]God
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Standing on the promises of [F]Christ the [C]Lord
[C]Bound to Him eter[G7]nally by love's strong [C]cord
[C]Overcoming daily with the [F]Spirit's [C]sword
Standing on the [G7]promises of [C]God
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Standing on the promises I [F]now can [C]see
[C]Perfect, present cleansing in the [G7]blood for [C]me
[C]Standing in the liberty where [F]Christ makes [C]free
Standing on the [G7]promises of [C]God
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
